{
  "description": "The START menu's third page (interface/mod_settings/mod_settings.py). Each name below is a key of menu_texts: the text, in the game's five languages.",
  "line": {"value": {"name": "mod_settings", "help": "mod_settings_help"}, "description": "The first row of the third page and the description shown while the cursor is on it. The page's other rows are the game's \"- - - - -\" line."},
  "entries": {
    "value": [{"name": "menu_graphics", "help": "menu_graphics_help", "opens": {"entries": [{"option": "cheat_3d_mode"}, {"option": "cheat_no_bloom_dof"}, {"option": "cheat_fps"}, {"option": "cheat_fov"}]}}, {"name": "menu_gameplay", "help": "menu_gameplay_help", "opens": {"entries": [{"option": "touchless_target"}, {"option": "hold_a"}, {"option": "fast_text"}, {"option": "fast_gathering"}, {"option": "camera_speed"}, {"name": "menu_camera", "help": "menu_camera_help", "opens": {"entries": [{"option": "modern_camera"}, {"option": "modern_camera_speed"}, {"option": "modern_camera_acceleration"}]}}, {"option": "horn_songs"}]}}, {"name": "menu_other", "help": "menu_other_help", "opens": {"entries": [{"name": "menu_damage", "help": "menu_damage_help", "opens": {"entries": [{"option": "damage_numbers"}, {"option": "damage_numbers_other"}, {"option": "damage_numbers_style"}, {"option": "damage_numbers_size"}, {"option": "damage_numbers_duration"}]}}, {"option": "cheat_net_fix"}, {"option": "cheat_raw_unbloat"}, {"option": "box_equipment"}, {"option": "system_keyboard"}, {"option": "skip_death_camera"}, {"option": "skip_monster_intro"}]}}, {"name": "aspect_ratio", "help": "aspect_ratio_help", "aspect": true, "opens": {"title": "aspect_ratio", "screen": "aspect_list"}}],
    "description": "The small list that Mod Settings opens, in order, 1 to 10 rows (the game's small list shows 5: a list of more has a second page, and the pager at pager_place says which). A row has its name and its description and what A opens: another small list ({\"entries\": [rows]}, whose B comes back to this row), a screen of the code ({\"title\": a text, \"screen\": aspect_list}), or an option's list of values ({\"option\": key} alone: its name, description and title come from `options`). A row with \"aspect\" is left out unless the aspect ratio's switch is on; an option the player's game cannot have is left out, and so is a list left with no row. All the lists together may have 6 lists and 40 rows (the code's data block, mod_settings.py MAX_LISTS and MAX_TABLE)."
  },
  "pager_place": {"value": [310, 22], "description": "Where a list's page number goes (a big list's, and a small list's of two pages, which then stands in for the menu's own), x and y in the top screen's layout: the place the game gives its own big lists."},
  "ten_row_raise": {"value": 28, "description": "In single-screen mode, how many pixels up a small list of more than five rows goes from its place beside the page's first row, so that its tenth row stays clear of the description's place at the bottom left (the list from y 34 to 222, the place from y 196.25: 2 pixels apart). The list goes no higher than the screen's top (y 6)."},
  "save_zone": {"value": {"offset": 74976, "magic": "RADL", "version": 1}, "description": "Where a character keeps the mod's choices: 48 bytes at this offset of the save data (0x124E0; the data starts 0x5C into the save object and the file holds its first 0x12600 bytes), which no code of the game reads. A character without the magic has none yet. The aspect ratio is its byte 9, the options' bytes 10 and up (`options`)."},
  "menu_texts": {
    "value": [
